      "writtenOn": "2015-08-18T23:29:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we return POWER_G3 we force shutdown by asserting PMIC_SLP_SUS_L. That prevents a true G3 startup because the part never enters deep S5 or S3 from a G3. It can only enter deep S5 or S3 from S0.\n\nPMIC_SLP_SUS_L is GPIO_OUT_LOW as default value. As that signal is the enable for the primary rails we never leave \"G3\" (DSW but no primary).",
      "parentUuid": "04b861a5_9cc007fa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "ee32f009aa51423de425a42a62d1268bd60914bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64591d73_4e4b857e",
        "filename": "power/skylake.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 193,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000100
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-08-19T00:18:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But until we return POWER_G3 here we have allowed the PCH to come out of DS while in the above delay loop, though I have no idea if that is a problem by itself since it is not forwarded to the PMIC yet.",
      "parentUuid": "c4156984_6eedc3b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "ee32f009aa51423de425a42a62d1268bd60914bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
